     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended dose of sertraline for adults is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is five times that. A dose this high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac effects such as QT prolongation. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, and that applies to a correctly dosed order too.\n\nIf a clinician needs this order, they can enter it themselves or confirm the intended dose with me. If the intended dose is 100 mg or another dose within the usual range of 25 to 200 mg daily, I can enter it once the prescriber confirms it. If this came from an existing request, please check the source with the prescriber."
      }
