     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the concerns, because you've told me you aren't a clinician and aren't the prescriber. A dose of 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended dose, so it needs confirmation from a licensed prescriber.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n\n- **If the order is real:** the prescriber should contact pharmacy and enter or verify it directly. Pharmacy will probably ask for the clinical reason for a dose this far above the usual range.\n- **If the dose is a mistake:** the prescriber can give me the correct dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily. I can enter that order once they confirm it.\n- **If you're unsure where the request came from:** please go back to the source and check before anything is ordered.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as a prescriber confirms the dose."
      }
